module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.GlobalGeneration
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.GenerationNecessary
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceSections.Basic

/-!
# The cover of the test scheme by the degree-one images of a quotient pair

A pair of Tag 01O4 is an invertible sheaf `ℒ` on a scheme `f : T ⟶ S` over the base together
with a graded map whose degree-one part

  `f^*𝒜₁ ⟶ ℒ`

is an epimorphism — `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.pairDegreeOneMap`, epi by
`epi_pairDegreeOneMap`. The chart construction
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization.toRelativeProjOfPair` needs more than
epimorphy: it needs
an actual open cover of `T` on each member of which some *named* section coming from degree one
is a basis of `ℒ`, because that is the section whose inverse the dehomogenization divides by.

This file produces that cover whenever `𝒜₁` is generated by global sections. Three facts compose
to give it:

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.pullbackGeneratingSections` carries generating
  sections of `𝒜₁` to generating sections of `f^*𝒜₁`;
* `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.ofEpi` carries those along the epimorphism to generating
  sections of `ℒ`;
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceSections.iSup_nonvanishingOpen_eq_top` says the nonvanishing loci of a
  generating family of an invertible sheaf cover the scheme.

So the cover is indexed by the generating family of `𝒜₁`, and on the member indexed by `i` the
basis is the image of the `i`-th generator — which is the shape the chart consumes.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.pairGeneratingSections`: **the generating sections
  of `ℒ` induced by generating sections of `𝒜₁`**, namely their images under the degree-one
  part of the pair's graded map.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.epi_sheafOfModules_pairDegreeOneMap`: the pair's
  degree-one surjectivity, read in the category `SheafOfModules T.ringCatSheaf` rather than in
  the copy `T.Modules`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.pairGeneratingSections_s`: the induced section is
  the image of the generator, with no comparison map in between.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.iSup_nonvanishingChart_pairGeneratingSections_eq_top`:
  **the cover.** The nonvanishing loci of the induced sections are all of `T`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.exists_nonvanishing_pairGeneratingSections`: the
  pointwise form — every point of the test scheme lies in one of them.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.isIso_over_nonvanishingChart_pairGeneratingSections`:
  on each member of the cover the induced section trivializes `ℒ`. This is Tag 01CY at the
  section the member was cut out by, and it is the second half of what the chart needs.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules T` and `SheafOfModules T.ringCatSheaf` have the same objects
and the same morphisms but distinct `Category` instances; the field `F1Pair.degreeOneSurjective`
lives in the former and `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.ofEpi` consumes the latter.
`epi_sheafOfModules_pairDegreeOneMap` rebuilds the epimorphism from its left-cancellation
property, which is the same proposition on both sides because the hom-types agree.

Invertibility of `ℒ` is the field `F1Pair.invertible`, not an instance, and is introduced with
`haveI` wherever the nonvanishing-locus API needs it.

Global generation of `𝒜₁` is a hypothesis rather than a consequence: quasi-coherence of `𝒜₁`
gives generating sections only *locally* on the base, the passage to global sections being the
reduction to an affine cover of `S`. The hypothesis holds over an affine base, where `𝒜₁` is the
sheaf associated to a module and its elements generate.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01B3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01B3)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceSections

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1

universe u

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} {A : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S} {TA : TensorAlgebras.{u}}
  {T : Scheme.{u}} {f : T ⟶ S} (P : F1Pair A TA f)

/-! ### The degree-one surjection, in the category generating sections are stated for -/

/-- **The pair's degree-one surjectivity, read in `SheafOfModules T.ringCatSheaf`.** The two
copies of the category have the same morphisms, so left cancellation transports verbatim. -/
public theorem epi_sheafOfModules_pairDegreeOneMap :
    @Epi (SheafOfModules.{u} T.ringCatSheaf) inferInstance _ _ (pairDegreeOneMap A TA P) :=
  ⟨(epi_pairDegreeOneMap A TA P).left_cancellation⟩

/-! ### The generating sections of the invertible sheaf -/

/-- **The sections of `ℒ` that a generating family of `𝒜₁` induces**: the images of the pulled
back generators under the degree-one part of the pair's graded map. They generate `ℒ`, because
pullback preserves generation and the degree-one part is an epimorphism. -/
public def pairGeneratingSections (σ : (A.piece 1).GeneratingSections) :
    P.L.GeneratingSections :=
  haveI := epi_sheafOfModules_pairDegreeOneMap P
  (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.pullbackGeneratingSections f (A.piece 1) σ).ofEpi
    (pairDegreeOneMap A TA P)

/-- The induced generating family of `ℒ` is indexed by the given generating family of `𝒜₁`. -/
@[simp]
public theorem pairGeneratingSections_I (σ : (A.piece 1).GeneratingSections) :
    (pairGeneratingSections P σ).I = σ.I :=
  rfl

/-- The induced section at an index is the image of the pulled-back generator under the pair's
degree-one map, with no comparison in between. -/
public theorem pairGeneratingSections_s (σ : (A.piece 1).GeneratingSections) (i : σ.I) :
    (pairGeneratingSections P σ).s i =
      SheafOfModules.sectionsMap (pairDegreeOneMap A TA P)
        ((Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.pullbackGeneratingSections f
          (A.piece 1) σ).s i) :=
  rfl

/-! ### The cover -/

/-- **The cover of the test scheme on which a degree-one image is a basis.** When `𝒜₁` is
generated by global sections, the loci on which the induced sections of `ℒ` do not vanish are
all of `T`.

On the member indexed by `i` the sheaf `ℒ` is trivialized by the image of the `i`-th generator,
which is the datum the dehomogenization chart of Tag 01O4 divides by. -/
public theorem iSup_nonvanishingChart_pairGeneratingSections_eq_top
    (σ : (A.piece 1).GeneratingSections) :
    haveI := P.invertible
    (⨆ i : σ.I, nonvanishingChart P.L ((pairGeneratingSections P σ).s i)) = ⊤ :=
  have := P.invertible
  iSup_nonvanishingOpen_eq_top P.L (pairGeneratingSections P σ)

/-- The pointwise form of the cover: every point of the test scheme lies in the nonvanishing
locus of the image of some generator of `𝒜₁`. -/
public theorem exists_nonvanishing_pairGeneratingSections
    (σ : (A.piece 1).GeneratingSections) (t : T) :
    haveI := P.invertible
    ∃ i : σ.I, t ∈ nonvanishingChart P.L ((pairGeneratingSections P σ).s i) :=
  have := P.invertible
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_generatingSection_nonvanishing P.L
    (pairGeneratingSections P σ) t

/-- **On each member of the cover the invertible sheaf is trivialized by the induced section.**
Tag 01CY for a scheme, at the section the member was cut out by: the morphism `𝒪 ⟶ ℒ` that
multiplies by the image of the `i`-th generator is an isomorphism over its own nonvanishing
locus, identifying the restriction of `ℒ` there with the structure sheaf. -/
public theorem isIso_over_nonvanishingChart_pairGeneratingSections
    (σ : (A.piece 1).GeneratingSections) (i : σ.I) :
    haveI := P.invertible
    IsIso ((P.L.unitHomEquiv.symm ((pairGeneratingSections P σ).s i)).over
      (nonvanishingChart P.L ((pairGeneratingSections P σ).s i))) :=
  have := P.invertible
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.Scheme.isIso_over_nonvanishingOpen T P.L
    ((pairGeneratingSections P σ).s i)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1

end
